# Third-party licenses

Lurkn itself is MIT-licensed — see [LICENSE](LICENSE). It is built on the work
below, each under its own license, and every copy of Lurkn carries these
notices with it.

The Rust part is generated by [cargo-about](https://github.com/EmbarkStudios/cargo-about)
from the dependency tree; run `just licenses` after changing dependencies.

## Not from Rust crates

| What | Where in Lurkn | License |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [Svelte](https://github.com/sveltejs/svelte) | the interface | MIT |
| [@tauri-apps/api](https://github.com/tauri-apps/tauri), plugin-clipboard-manager, plugin-opener | the interface's bridge to Rust | MIT or Apache-2.0 |
| [Material Icons](https://github.com/google/material-design-icons) `live_tv` | the watch button | Apache-2.0 |
| [Lucide](https://github.com/lucide-icons/lucide) `arrow-left-from-line`, `arrow-right-to-line` | the synced window's chat arrows | ISC |

The MIT, Apache-2.0 and ISC texts below apply to these as well.

